{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545640-horror-vs-urban-fantasy-what-s-the-best-balance-for-curseborne","id":1545640,"title":"Horror vs. urban fantasy - What's the best balance for Curseborne?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-10T01:41:11-08:00","id":1545640,"title":"Horror vs. urban fantasy - What's the best balance for Curseborne?","content":"Angel, Buffy the Vampire Slayer, Dresden Files, Anita Blake (before it became porn), Mercy Thompson, Witchblade, Warrior Nun, Constantine (not Hellblazer), and other &quot;monsters and monster hunting media&quot; all have horror elements but are very much about being able to push back against the darkness. They're not coincidentally where the protagonists are capable of using the supernatural themselves and able to fight fire against fire.<br /> <br /> I think of these as urban fantasy.<br /> <br /> This is contrasted against Fright Night, Friday the 13th (series and films), Halloween, Alan Wake, SCP Foundation, Dracula, Twin Peaks, the X-Files, and other works where the protagonists may be able to banish the darkness for a time but are very squarely in the horror genre.<br /> <br /> We also have things that straddle the fence like Forever Night.<br /> <br /> I'm inclined to think this may just be a choice of table style but I'm curious how you think YOU would run it and it would run best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a T